[THOUGHT] The supervisor highlights that the prior biopsy was nondiagnostic and DIF was not performed. Given infancy onset, widespread pustules, high inflammatory markers, and positive GBS culture, the single most informative next step is a repeat, targeted skin biopsy of an active pustule with explicit requests for histologic detail plus immunopathology and special stains to distinguish pustular psoriasis/sterile neutrophilic dermatoses, IgA pemphigus/subcorneal pustular dermatosis, and occult infection. This will directly address the top critical data gaps (level/type of pustule, Kogoj spongiform pustules, neutrophilic infiltrate, special stains) and guide further genetic and infectious workup.

[TEST] Repeat punch skin biopsy of an active pustule (include edge + center and a follicular unit if possible) for:
- Histopathology (H&E) with explicit commentary on pustule level (subcorneal vs intraepidermal vs follicular), presence of spongiform pustules of Kogoj, neutrophilic vs eosinophilic infiltrate, and psoriasiform/acanthotic changes;
- Direct immunofluorescence (DIF) on perilesional skin (evaluate for intercellular IgA/IgG/IgM/C3);
- Special stains on tissue: Gram stain and PAS (or GMS) for organisms;
- Send tissue for repeat bacterial (aerobic/anaerobic) and fungal cultures.

[THOUGHT] The repeat biopsy with DIF and cultures that I ordered is the single most decisive missing data point to distinguish pustular psoriasis/sterile neutrophilic disease from IgA pemphigus or persistent infection. I need the full biopsy report (H&E details), DIF findings, special stains, and tissue culture results to form a conclusive differential.

[TEST] Provide the complete results of the repeat punch skin biopsy (edge + center) including:
- Histopathology (H&E) with description of pustule level — subcorneal vs intraepidermal vs follicular — presence/absence of spongiform pustules of Kogoj, neutrophilic vs eosinophilic infiltrate, and any psoriasiform/acanthotic changes;
- Direct immunofluorescence (DIF) results (IgA, IgG, IgM, C3 pattern);
- Special stains (Gram, PAS/GMS) results;
- Tissue bacterial and fungal culture results and sensitivities.

